🔑 Key Formula

Alligation Rule

Cheaper : Dearer = (Dearer Price − Mean Price) : (Mean Price − Cheaper Price)

💡 Example

A mixture is made by mixing a ₹40/kg item with a ₹60/kg item to get a mixture worth ₹50/kg.

Cheaper : Dearer
= (60 − 50) : (50 − 40)
= 10 : 10
= 1 : 1

Therefore, the two items should be mixed in the ratio 1 : 1.
